181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 99 0 R
/T (The ARC Robotics Competition \(formerly RoboMaster North America\) plays like a real-world crossover between a First-Person Shooter \(FPS\) and a Multiplayer Online Battle Arena \(MOBA\). Two teams face off in high-speed tactical matches, deploying fleets of custom-built, semi-autonomous, and fully autonomous robots. Operators control these machines with no direct line of sight to the robots, steering and aiming entirely through real-time FPV camera feeds.)
/E (The ARC Robotics Competition \(formerly RoboMaster North America\) plays like a real-world crossover between a First-Person Shooter \(FPS\) and a Multiplayer Online Battle Arena \(MOBA\). Two teams face off in high-speed tactical matches, deploying fleets of custom-built, semi-autonomous, and fully autonomous robots. Operators control these machines with no direct line of sight to the robots, steering and aiming entirely through real-time FPV camera feeds.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 99 0 R
/T (To win, teams must coordinate different robot classes to capture strategic map objectives and defeat the opposing base. Hits are tracked instantly by pressure-sensitive armor plates connected to a digital referee system, which monitors hit points \(HP\) and electrical power limits in real time.)
/E (To win, teams must coordinate different robot classes to capture strategic map objectives and defeat the opposing base. Hits are tracked instantly by pressure-sensitive armor plates connected to a digital referee system, which monitors hit points \(HP\) and electrical power limits in real time.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
